# The schema declares `legacy_posts`; the model is called Post. Nothing links
# them but a literal in the class body, and they live in different blobs — so
# the join is a tree question.
#
# It is also the one relation demand-loading cannot work out lazily: a per-name
# load never sees the whole method table, so the carrier→model map is settled
# up front from the `table_name` definitions alone. This case is here because
# that is the part of the laziness most likely to rot silently.
#
# `owner` is the *carrier* (`LegacyPost`), not the model — only the lookup key
# is re-mapped onto Post. That is long-standing behaviour and arguably wrong to
# report, since no such class exists; pinned as-is so changing it is a decision.
def post.rb:7:7 status=resolved owner=LegacyPost via=local:new site=db/schema.rb:1
